  "Para 1 (Midrash quotation, end): the source text reads \"עזרי !עעם ה'\" - a corrupt word; Bereishis Rabbah 68:2 and Tehillim 121:2 read \"מֵעִם\". Printed reading kept unvocalized, with the correction [מֵעִם] in brackets.",
  "Para 1 (on 'and grace to your throat'): \"וכן בנשון חכמים\" - typo for \"בלשון\" (in the language of). Printed reading kept, with [בִּלְשׁוֹן] in brackets.",
  "Para 1: \"לית אנא מובד\" here vs. \"מוביד\" in para 2 - spelling variants of the same Aramaic word (Bereishis Rabbah reads מובד); both kept as printed.",
  "Para 1: \"לא שהיה כדי\" - read as כדאי (worthy), as in Bereishis Rabbah 29 on Noach; kept as printed and vocalized כְּדַי.",
  "Para 1 (Zohar II 54a): \"א\"ז\" expanded as אָלֶף זַיִן (the two letters of the word אָז), since the Zohar goes on to explain the alef and the zayin; uncertain expansion.",
  "Para 1: the reference \"(נדה עב.)\" for the term גרגרן could not be confirmed; kept as printed.",
  "Para 2: \"(ברכות כז:)\" - the teaching that Yaakov instituted Arvit from 'ויפגע במקום' is in Berachos 26b; כז: may be a misprint (unless it points to the discussion of Arvit on 27b). Kept as printed.",
  "Para 2: Tehillim 127:2 reads שֵׁנָא in the Masoretic text; the print has שנה, kept and vocalized שֵׁנָה.",
  "Names given as acronyms (רש\"י, רמב\"ן, האריז\"ל) are kept as names (רַשִׁ״י, רַמְבַּ״ן, הָאֲרִ״י) with the honorific ז\"ל expanded."
